WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.520
It's that time again. Welcome to Tesla Shorts Time, Episode 556 for July 29th, 2026. I'm Patrick,

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:15.080
coming to you from Vancouver. Here's what you need to know about Tesla today. Tesla's cybercab

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:22.300
now ships with a factory integrated Starlink V5 terminal that enables 4,000 streaming and constant

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:30.400
fsd updates during unsupervised rides. Tesla has integrated the Starlink V5 terminal directly into

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:36.700
every cybercab at the factory. The terminal sits hidden inside the body and appears only in computer

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:44.460
generated diagrams released so far. It supports speeds above 375 megabits per second and allows

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:51.100
passengers to watch 4k streaming video while the vehicle operates without a driver. Elon Musk

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:57.160
stated that the constant connection also delivers the latest full self-driving AI fixes to the fleet

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:04.040
in real time. This marks the first high-volume Tesla model to ship with native SpaceX satellite hardware.

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:10.040
Production at Giga, Texas is already underway, though most early units remain in engineering

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:16.440
testing. The same connectivity that keeps robotaxies online also underscores Tesla's growing

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:24.140
need for massive, reliable power. Tesla's decision to embed Starlink V5 hardware in every cybercab

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:30.420
from the factory line changes the unit economics of robotaxie operations in a way that is easy

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:36.780
to overlook. Instead of relying on ground-based cellular networks that can drop in rural corridors

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:43.780
or during peak congestion, each vehicle carries a direct satellite link capable of sustained multi-hundred

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:49.660
megabits throughput. That link keeps the car connected for software updates and ride-hailing

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:56.020
dispatch even when traditional coverage is absent, removing one variable that otherwise requires

00:01:56.020 --> 00:02:02.760
redundant systems or root restrictions. The same hardware also turns the robotaxie into a permanent

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:09.100
high-volume customer for SpaceX's satellite constellation. With production targets measured in

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:14.360
millions of units, the arrangement creates a captive demand stream that is difficult for competitors

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:20.760
to replicate without similar cross-company ownership. It compresses the cost of connectivity into the

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:26.820
vehicle bill of materials rather than leaving it as an ongoing operating expense that varies by region

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:33.600
and carrier. Yet the approach carries its own constraint. Any latency or outage on the satellite side

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:39.800
now affects the entire fleet rather than isolated vehicles. Tesla must therefore treat satellite

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:46.980
performance as a core reliability specification alongside cameras, compute, and motors. Tesla has

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:53.380
contracted for 90% of the output from a major Arizona Solar Plus storage project to power its

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:59.720
growing AI compute needs. The company also signed a separate power purchase agreement with contour

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:06.800
global for one terawatt hour per year from project sterling. Both deals target clean power for AI

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:13.540
compute clusters and manufacturing rather than residential use. The shift reflects rising electricity

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:19.680
demand from training clusters and inference hardware. Construction and interconnection timelines

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:25.120
were not detailed in the announcements. This connects directly to ongoing supply questions

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:31.680
around the same AI push. Elon Musk highlighted Micron technology twice in the recent earnings call.

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:37.900
He pointed to ongoing constraints in high bandwidth memory needed for Tesla's AI training clusters.

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:44.340
The comments underscore how memory supply has become a bottleneck alongside GPUs as

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:50.660
Tesla's Scales Cortex and Dojo systems. Investors are watching whether the praise signals new

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:56.420
supply agreements or simply acknowledges the tightness. No new agreements were announced during the

00:03:56.420 --> 00:04:03.700
call itself. Tesla is deploying distributed megapods as part of its broader AI compute scaling plan.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:09.800
The approach spreads hardware across multiple sites rather than concentrating everything in a single

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:16.200
supercluster. This strategy is intended to improve resilience and speed up deployment of additional

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:22.900
capacity for both training and inference workloads. The world's largest car carrier departed Shanghai

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:29.240
loaded with enough Tesla vehicles to form a line more than 22 miles long if parked bumper to bumper.

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:35.660
The shipment reflects continued high volume exports from giga Shanghai even as global demand

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:42.520
patterns shift. Exact model mix was not disclosed but the scale shows the plants ongoing role in

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:48.720
supplying multiple markets. Tesla has begun offering the Powerwall 3 residential battery system

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:55.120
in Northern Ireland. The move expands the company's energy storage footprint in the UK and Ireland

00:04:55.120 --> 00:05:01.740
after earlier rollouts in Great Britain. Home owners now gain access to the latest generation hardware

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:08.480
paired with solar. Local installers are being onboarded to support the launch. Tesla has now delivered

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:15.200
more than 16,000 electric vehicles in Malaysia. The company is adding new supercharger sites and

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:21.980
emphasizing over-the-air capability as a core part of its local strategy. These moves come as Tesla

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:28.800
works to deepen its presence in Southeast Asia beyond initial market entry. Tesla's summer update

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:35.060
now allows drivers and passengers to join Google Meet, Microsoft Teams and Discord calls using

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:40.600
the cabin camera and microphones. The feature runs through the vehicle's existing connectivity

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:47.640
and is positioned as an extension of the infotainment system. It arrives alongside other software changes

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:54.240
in the same release cycle. Elon Musk has called Optimus potentially the largest product in Tesla's

00:05:54.240 --> 00:06:01.420
history. Current production data shows only limited prototype output at giga Texas. The dedicated

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:07.980
Optimus factory remains under construction with volume production still targeted for 2027 and beyond.

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:14.320
Observers are tracking whether early internal deployments will provide the first real volume signal.

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:21.200
Tesla Japan has activated free supercharging for owners in areas impacted by the recent earthquake.

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:27.620
The temporary measure applies at participating stations and is being communicated through local channels.

00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:33.500
It follows similar regional support actions the company has taken in past natural disasters.

